de  ecd you see a lot of extensive  information within these plots  we see a lot of cesium assignments  as well as site localization of where  the glycogen is along the peptide  backbone and you see we've got good  sequence coverage across the peptide  backbone as well as site localization of  the glycan  you look at another example of the g1f  glycopeptide or the following  glycopeptide shown here  we have our tic on the top of the nysma  triptych digest  as well as the corresponding cid and sms  spectrum  and again the cid msns section shows  mainly  cleavage of the sugar moieties of the  glycogen structure attached to peptides  we really don't see much information in  regards to the peptide backbone  cleavages  now if we perform the same analysis as  ecd  we see a lot of incentive information  regarding peptide backbone cleavage with  the cz and ion and sinus  as well as site localization of the  glycan moiety is on the peptide backbone  so we can see from rebecca's example  here that these specs can really be  quite complex and we're going to be  relying really heavily on our data  analysis software in order to extract as  much information as possible and really  minimize that manual interpretation  before i begin my name is cody schwarzer  and i work with rebecca newmission to  help develop some of the data analysis  workflows that we'll be using for the  exd so  now today i'm going to be sharing uh  just one of our options  and this allows for our raw exd data to  be incorporated directly into your  protein metrics pipelines  protein metrics or bios  as many of you may already be aware as a  vendor neutral software  it's used by many of our customers  already for day-to-day cqa analysis  and agilent already has a relationship  with protein metrics as we use their hcp  tools as part of our own wholesale  protein workflow  what we're proposing here is that we  also incorporate ptm  to process our exv data  now the workflow is fairly  straightforward the data is 